Given origin (x0,y0), direction (dx,dy) unit, cell size c, grid origin (-R, +R) with y decreasing as j increases:
i = floor((x + R)/c), j = floor((R - y)/c)
stepX = dx > 0 ? 1 : -1; stepY = dy > 0 ? -1 : 1 (since j increases downward in y)
tMaxX = distance along ray to next x boundary; tDeltaX = c / |dx|
similarly for y.

Loop: 
  check current cell (i,j) at t (entry t).
  advance to the smaller of tMaxX/tMaxY, update i or j, and t.
  if out of bounds → stop.

